A peaceful elderly woman's weathered hands resting on a worn wooden kitchen table, with a simple ceramic plate holding the delicate skeleton of a small fish, bones picked clean. Late afternoon golden light streams through a window with sheer curtains, casting long shadows. In the background, slightly blurred, hints of both old-world elements—a traditional woven basket, dried herbs hanging—and modern touches like a sleek rice cooker. The scene evokes the passage of time, wisdom passed between generations, and the quiet dignity of a life fully lived. Style of Vincent van Gogh: expressive brushstrokes with rich impasto texture, swirling warm yellows and deep blues, emotional depth in ordinary domestic objects, the light rendered with characteristic radiating energy, creating a sense of reverence and gentle melancholy in this humble kitchen scene.
